  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The gold coins of Samudragupta are important historical sources from the
    Gupta period. The obverse, or front side, presents the emperor as a powerful
    ruler, while the reverse side uses religious and artistic symbols. In this module,
    the coin shows Samudragupta with a bow, inscriptions written in Brahmi script,
    and a reverse design featuring Goddess Lakshmi seated on a lotus. The gold material
    reflects the wealth and economic strength of the Gupta Empire. The peacock emblem
    represents beauty, dignity and royalty. Together, the portrait, inscription,
    deity, lotus and decorative motifs help us understand Gupta kingship, religion,
    prosperity, art and culture.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
